---
profile: production
exclude_paths:
  - collections/
  - tests/fixtures/
# Role-default vars are referenced directly by playbooks and localhost tests
# (e.g. secrets_file, deploy_base), so the role-name prefix convention does not
# fit this layout. The secret-env values in group_vars are deliberately named
# after the exact process-environment NAMES they carry (UPPER_SNAKE, e.g.
# SOLANA_RPC_URL) so stack_deploy can extract them by name — that is the whole
# point of the stack_env_vars map. Skip only those two stylistic rules; the rest
# of the production profile holds.
skip_list:
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]
  - var-naming[pattern]
